# Paths that scripts/check_sensitive_files.py would flag but which are safe to
# share. One path per line, scoped to one rule (path:rule) wherever possible,
# each with a comment saying who decided and why.
#
# This file exists so that overriding the check leaves a reviewable trace in the
# repository. If it grows without comments, the check is being worked around
# rather than used.

# The check's own specification. It has to contain the things it detects: a
# fixture script with a private header, and a fake cluster path.
# Reviewed 2026-10-25.
